-- title:
--   Newton step for Fontaine's w-series at p=2
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime with $p = 2$, and $d$ a natural number. Let $a_{i,n} \in \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,d$, $n \in \mathbb{N}$) be multivariate power series with vanishing constant coefficient, and let $Da_{i,n,j}$ be the formal partial derivative $\partial a_{i,n}/\partial X_j$, specified coefficientwise by the requirement that the coefficient of $m$ in $Da_{i,n,j}$ be $(m_j + 1)$ times the coefficient of $m + e_j$ in $a_{i,n}$. Let $g$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is complete and separated for the $(p)$-adic filtration, let $x_1,\dots,x_d \in g$ lie in the radical of the ideal $(p)$, let $y_1,\dots,y_d \in g$ be arbitrary, and fix $i$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$. Writing $S_N(z) = \sum_{n<N} p^{-n} \, a_{i,n}(z)^{p^n}$ for the partial sum of Fontaine's $w$-series, formed in the localisation $g[1/p]$ with $p^{-n}$ the $n$-th power of the inverse of the (unit) image of $p$, and with all power series evaluated $(p)$-adically, the assertion is that
--   $$S_N(x + p y) - S_N(x) - p\Bigl(\sum_j \bigl(\textstyle\sum_{n<N} a_{i,n}(x)^{p^n-1} (Da_{i,n,j})(x)\bigr) y_j + \sum_j \bigl(\sum_{1 \le n < N} a_{i,n}(x)^{p^n-2} (Da_{i,n,j})(x)^2\bigr) y_j^2\Bigr)$$
--   lies in the $g$-submodule of $g[1/p]$ generated by the image of $p^2$; the exponents $p^n - 1$ and $p^n - 2$ are truncated natural subtraction, and the quadratic sum starts at $n = 1$ accordingly.
--
--   This is the finite-level Newton (second-order Taylor) step for Fontaine's $w$-series in the exceptional case $p = 2$, where the binomial expansion of $(u + 2v)^{2^n}$ leaves, after division by $2^n$, a square term that survives modulo $4$; the linear coefficient is the Jacobian of the $a_{i,n}$ and the quadratic coefficient is the Frobenius-twisted square of its entries. It is used in the construction of the Fontaine lift, through [`Deformation.FontaineLift.existsUnique_sub_mem_and_wSeries_adicEval_eq_of_isUnit_linearPart`](thm.html#Deformation.FontaineLift.existsUnique_sub_mem_and_wSeries_adicEval_eq_of_isUnit_linearPart), where unique solvability of the step modulo $4$ requires the extra normal-form hypothesis on the linear part at $p = 2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_PLoc_wPartialSum_adicEval_add_sub_sub_algebraMap_mul_add_mem_powSub_two.lean

import Mathlib
